From 2292fa37e716f48b54cf09fc8fffc3da65f9731c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 04:04:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Rebuild SAM-FracTAL fusion and post-processing; add
 DINOv3/DINOv2-FracTAL

SAM-FracTAL (notebooks/SAM-FractalResUNET):
- Replace bottleneck cross-attention (no positional encoding, gate stuck at
  0.012) with spatially aligned GatedFusion at three U-Net levels; fusion
  strength starts at 0.5, trains at the normal LR, no weight decay
- Build boundary targets from instance ids so edges shared by touching
  fields are supervised; per-field normalised distance target
- Train on native-resolution random crops, targets computed after the
  geometric augmentations; padding ignored in all losses
- Thinner boundaries: BCE pos_weight 20 -> 3 plus soft Dice, CE boundary
  weight 12 -> 3
- Select checkpoints on field-level F1 (watershed + IoU>0.5 matching),
  2px-tolerance boundary F1, early stopping, bf16/fp16 AMP
- Grid-search watershed thresholds on validation, store them in best.pt,
  report test-set metrics
- Inference: seeded watershed on the distance/boundary heads instead of
  boundary cut + buffer + NMS; padded tiling (fixes zeroed image border),
  batched tiles, flip TTA, pixel-exact georeferenced polygons, crs=None
  for non-georeferenced images
- Read the Roboflow key from Colab secrets instead of hardcoding it

DINO-FracTAL (notebooks/DINO-FractalResUNET, new):
- Same U-Net, losses and post-processing with a frozen DINOv3 ViT-L/16
  SAT-493M backbone (multi-depth tokens -> three fusion levels), falling
  back to DINOv3 ViT-B/16 and then DINOv2 ViT-B/14 when the gated DINOv3
  weights are not accessible

